       }
      ],
      "text": "**For a brief trip outside, you probably don’t need a mask if you’re generally healthy.** But Singapore’s air was unhealthy today: at 7pm, NEA reported 1-hour PM2.5 readings of 106–198 µg/m³ (elevated to high). Avoid strenuous outdoor exercise; if you’ll be outside for a long time—or you’re in a more vulnerable group—consider a well-fitting N95/KN95 and check NEA’s latest 1-hour PM2.5 reading first. A regular surgical mask won’t filter fine haze particles effectively. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-17-october-2026))",
